					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-126348#post-2420779</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-126348/scp-504#post-2420779</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 10 Dec 2015 21:17:15 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Suromit</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2361172</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>While these little buggers were not my introduction to the SCPs, they hold a near and dear place in my heart. Not only because they're a wonderfully humorous idea, but they were the favorite entry to a late friend of mine, who many times deserved to be clocked by an instance of 504.</p> <p>Also, I highly disagree with those saying this should be reclassified as a -J. -Js are jokes in of themselves; silly humor from the get-go that are written to be wholly tongue-in-cheek to begin with, with many not even having actual anomalous properties. This is a legitimate mainlist SCP that would actually pose a very real threat to the general populace if it were not contained by the foundation.</p> <p>I mean, lord, could you imagine if people accidentally grew these in their back yard? Or their window sill? Individual circumstances are variable, but depending on the tomato's range of target acquisition, the danger it would pose is VERY real.</p> <p>That's a good idea for a test actually. &quot;What is the range at which puns are lethal?&quot;</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-126348#post-2332560</guid>
				<title>Staff Post - Open</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-126348/scp-504#post-2332560</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2015 18:30:07 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Zyn</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1404533</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Noting that a recent change was reverted (thanks to Salty Cupcake for doing so and notifying me via PM) as it was a log addition done without permission by the original author or staff.</p> <p>Readers, remember that grammatical edits are appreciated, but if a page is not tagged with &quot;collaboration&quot; only the original author may add new entries into the corresponding test logs. As such, while punctuation and spelling can be corrected, you should obtain author permission prior to adding new content yourself.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-126348#post-2252705</guid>
				<title>Staff Post</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-126348/scp-504#post-2252705</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 18 Mar 2015 03:47:29 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Zyn</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1404533</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Reverted a recent change, since &quot;shuriken&quot; is an acceptable plural. Adding an s is a Western convention; in Japanese the plural is the same as the singular.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
